ite a bit it  marked a return to the place he once  worked as a teenager sweeping up after  the crowds did you ever look up at the  grand old opry and think to myself  going to be there  it's such a legendary place that i don't  even know if i thought  if i ever it's it's like too far beyond  your dreams and now you you think in the  reverse you know if it doesn't go well  up there you can always come back and  i think they're gonna make me sweep  after the show  part of the deal but making people laugh  has always come naturally to nate  perhaps because it runs in the family  his father stephen was a clown i was  born he was a clown it was never weird  to me i thought everybody's dad was a  clown  i remember his first joke his first joke  this guy's sitting there and he goes  waiter there's a fly in my soup  and the waiter goes don't worry the  spider on the spoon will get it  and nathan laughed i mean we're like  tears coming down his eyes he's laughing  at this joke he's five and a half years  old then he explains to me why it's  funny he said don't you this is what  makes that such a great funny joke  and i mean it didn't but a light should  have come on right then what kid thinks  about why something's funny  on the night we visited dad was also one  of the opening ads it's got to be  elmore's glue okay a little goofiness  followed by a lot of hearts i'm just so  proud of my family  and i had to follow him doing good and  then it's emotional  and then i got to go up and like get and  i got to dig myself out of that hole  i mean you cry because he's your son but  also because  he's doing what you once wanted to do  yeah yeah that's very very very true do  you have a theory for why nate seems to  be connecting so much right now people  can relate to his comedy and they relate  to there and he's not a joke teller he's  a storyteller yeah and i think people  sense what he's telling them is really  happening too and it is i see a dead  horse  just laid out in this guy's yard nate  bar bargetsi's humor reminds us that  we're all probably a little more  clueless than we'd like to admit  so i learned that horses  lay down to sleep  i did not know that and that's  okay  where are you trying to go  your i guess ultimate goal would be like  when people talk about like because i  mean it's hard to narrow and be like one  person's like the greatest there's you  know prior chappelle carl and seinfeld  you get all these kind of names burr  uh but you just want to be mentioned i  think with  uh  with the people at the top like that's  that's the ultimate  goal that i think for me is a stand-up  so so nate's one of the funniest and one  of my favorite people to have on tv in  my household he was a very soothing and  hilarious presence through the  coronavirus lockdowns uh and so it was  thrilling for me to be able to introduce  him to a wider audience but i i thank  you for the introduction both you guys  knew who he was i had never heard of him  before it reminds me of sebastian  manoskalco i like humor that's relatable  that's funny yeah and clean and i just  think i love his delivery yeah i'm now  going to look at the netflix stuff yeah  go back to it everyone should tennessee  kids tony there's nothing like relatable  comedy be right we'll be right back

